  "worked_solution": "First, we apply the power of product rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n{({5}^{3}\\times 3)}^{4}={({5}^{3})}^{4}\\times {3}^{4}\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite the first factor using the power rule for exponents, and simplify:\n\n$$\n{({5}^{3})}^{4}\\times {3}^{4}={5}^{3\\cdot 4}\\times {3}^{4}={5}^{12}\\times {3}^{4}\n$$",
